                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "SPOILERS!!!!\r\n\r\n\r\nIt is always the moment I take my eyes off you that you scamper off to the nearest crime with all the zeal of a puppy with no lead.\r\n-Pendleton, Grand Ending\r\n\r\nyep that pretty much sums up the FL. I don't recommend this because it get boring in the middle and the plot feels a bit stretched out. it doesn't end here either as there are still unsolved mysteries. but I did enjoy some moments though. Lupine's route is short and pretty straightforward so play his route last. the rest just feel drawn out. also if you're looking into very serious detective story, this is not it. most of the time, they often forget they're even detectives and the FL hoarded that achievement. if you want to play to kill time, go for it otherwise it's up to you.\r\n\r\nPS. tbh, every FL's problem could have been prevented if Pendleton and Sarah Marple had been one of the candidates.\r\n\r\nPPS. Jack's route in a nutshell\r\nMC: You have scary eyes like you haven't slept for days. (lick her lips dramatically like Bella Swan) That Cockney accent is music to my ears. These nonchalant expressions. (making a face like having diarrhea) You look at everyone with sharp, killer eyes. What are you?\r\nJack: Nuffink o' yer bizness\r\nMC: How long have you been like this?\r\nJack: Since I was a little 'un\r\nMC: I know what you are.\r\nJack: Out wiv it then! Say it out 'loud, go on! \r\nMC: An assassin.\r\nJack: Ya shittin' yerself are ya?\r\nMC: No. \r\nJack: Then ask me the most bleedin' basic queshun: why do we do the 'it? \r\nMC: You won't hurt me.\r\n\r\n*'hoa hoa hoa hoaaaa' Twilight soundtrack in the background*",
